BT /F2 10 Tf 50 750 Td (Syllora Academic Repository | Course: CS301 Operating Systems) Tj 400 0 Td (Page 1 of 3) Tj -400 -25 Td /F2 16 Tf (CS301: Tanenbaum - Modern Operating Systems Excerpt) Tj 0 -30 Td /F1 11 Tf 16 TL T* /F2 13 Tf (Chapter 6: Deadlocks in Modern Operating Systems) Tj /F1 11 Tf T* (6.1 Resources and Preemptibility) Tj T* (In operating systems, a resource is an object that can be acquired, used, and released.) Tj T* (Resources can be preemptible \(like CPU or memory pages, which can be taken away without harm\)) Tj T* (or non-preemptible \(like dedicated Blu-ray burners or database row locks\).) Tj T* (Deadlocks typically involve non-preemptible resources where forcing preemption) Tj T* (would corrupt system state or lead to race conditions.) Tj T* ET
endstream
